Yea, sorry about the code craziness.  I thought that part seems odd, but wasn't sure how to fix it.  The original multiselect-demo.js file I upload defines the function as:

  function RapacheLP() {
             <%
             Rfunction<-function(){

             aa<-ifelse(!is.null(POST$ fnumber), fromJSON(as.character(POST$fnumber)), 1)

            bb<-ifelse(!is.null(POST$Snumber), fromJSON(as.character(POST$snumber)), 9999)
            cc<-aa+bb
            return(toJSON(cc))
            } %>
            var summing = <%= Rfunction() %>;
            return(summing);
   };

This function is called in the form submission event handler.  But it seems like the function is getting processed through R initially before the form is submitted and then those values are retained (i.e. it's not re-processed when the form is submitted and POST$fnumber and POST$snumber exist).  So I'm not sure how to make Rfunction get re-brewed every time the form is submitted....or is there a better way to do this?

